WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.426 --> 00:00:04.106
Unit two. Using a Mouse and Keyboard!

2
00:00:05.042 --> 00:00:09.571
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.621 --> 00:00:12.587
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.637 --> 00:00:17.000
Today we learn about Using a Mouse and Keyboard. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.684 --> 00:00:22.178
Click. Say it with me. Click!

6
00:00:25.723 --> 00:00:30.041
Double-click. Say it with me. Double-click!

7
00:00:33.525 --> 00:00:37.425
Drag. Say it with me. Drag!

8
00:00:40.916 --> 00:00:44.316
Type. Say it with me. Type!

9
00:00:47.821 --> 00:00:51.942
Letter key. Say it with me. Letter key!

10
00:00:55.407 --> 00:01:00.062
Space bar. Say it with me. Space bar!

11
00:01:03.599 --> 00:01:07.824
Enter key. Say it with me. Enter key!

12
00:01:11.311 --> 00:01:15.159
Cursor. Say it with me. Cursor!

13
00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:32.715
I use my mouse to click and drag things on the screen. I use the keyboard to type a letter or press the space bar. The cursor shows me where I am on the screen, and the enter key starts a new line.

14
00:01:32.765 --> 00:01:35.921
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:36.604 --> 00:01:42.339
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:42.389 --> 00:01:43.539
Drag!

17
00:01:44.412 --> 00:01:50.113
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:50.163 --> 00:01:51.459
Enter key!

19
00:01:52.529 --> 00:02:01.200
Did you know? The computer mouse got its name because its cord looked like a little tail, just like a real mouse!

20
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.808
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:14.244
Think and answer. What is the difference between a click and a double-click?

22
00:02:14.294 --> 00:02:15.485
Great answer!

23
00:02:16.544 --> 00:02:22.170
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:25.193
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

